The bootstrap runs on the lab host itself: bootstrap.sh clones this repository
onto the host and runs site.yml against localhost over the local connection,
which is why the only committed inventory is localhost.yml.

To run the same playbook from a workstation instead, write an inventory that
names the host and the SSH user the hardening role created (hcwadmin), and
pass it with -i. The playbook targets `all`, so nothing else changes:

    ansible-playbook -i inventory/remote.yml site.yml --vault-password-file /etc/hcw/ansible/vault-password -e @/etc/hcw/ansible/vault.yml

A remote inventory belongs on the workstation, not in the repository: it names
a real address, and this directory is committed.
